ingle. I'd keep B7 and B2 because they can combine with B4,B1 for possible chow B1-B3 (need B3) or B2-B4 (need B3,B4). But since B1 is terminal and I may discard it, maybe keep B2,B4,B7.\n\nSo first discard: F3.\n\n**Reason:**  \nDiscarding F3 removes an honor tile that is hard to meld (only one left unseen) and not part of any likely high-point pattern given my current hand, which already has two suited chows. Keeping only simples (W and B) offers more flexibility to form additional chows aiming for All Chows + All Simples patterns, and possibly Half Flush if I later draw more W tiles. F3 is also relatively safe given it has been discarded by other players before.\n\n**Answer:** Play F3"}
